# The three historical paper authors below are reference authors, not asserted
# software contributors. Repository URL, release DOI, version, and release date
# are deliberately omitted until they exist.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this software for the numerical work and the referenced 1993 article
  for the original scientific question. Use the release identifier when a
  versioned repository release is available.
title: "Propeller Chains Revisited: localized and collective molecular rotations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: MohammadHosseini
    given-names: AmirMohammad
    website: https://github.com/AMIRMOHAMMAD-OSS
abstract: >-
  A reproducible MMFF94 study of localized transition networks and specified
  synchronized torsion paths in compound 6 from Lindner, Grynszpan, and Biali
  (1993), with stationary-point, connectivity, symmetry, and convergence checks.
keywords:
  - molecular propellers
  - conformational transitions
  - molecular mechanics
  - transition states
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Lindner
        given-names: Ariel B.
      - family-names: Grynszpan
        given-names: Flavio
      - family-names: Biali
        given-names: Silvio E.
    title: >-
      Transmission of Internal Rotations: Correlated, Uncorrelated, and
      Localized Disrotatory Rotations in Propeller Chains
    journal: The Journal of Organic Chemistry
    year: 1993
    month: 11
    volume: "58"
    issue: "24"
    start: "6662"
    end: "6670"
    doi: 10.1021/jo00076a027
    url: https://doi.org/10.1021/jo00076a027
